Help Cure Cystic Fibrosis

The Cystic Fibrosis Foundation is hosting its annual Great Strides Walk on Saturday, May 19 at Hermann Park.  The event is the foundation's major, grassroots fundraising event, and $0.92 of every dollar raised in the walk goes directly to furthering research into more effective treatments for the disease.

Cystic Fibrosis is the most common fatal genetic disease in the Caucasian population today, affecting over 30,000 children and young adults in the United States.  The current median survival age for CF patients is 31 years.

If you would like more information on participating in the walk or sponsoring a walker, please contact Jeff Poche at X 6-9530.

