I am forwarding the agenda for ISDA's Annual General Meeting at the Omni
Shoreham Hotel April 3-6. Highlights include:

* Keynote Addresses by Senator Richard Lugar, William McDonough and
Peter Hancock and Jeffrey Skilling
* Global derivatives public policy panel re: current and future
regulatory developments in Europe and the United States.
* Plenary sessions covering Latin America and Asia, which will have a
regulatory and policy focus.
* Developing Products Panel  (weather, energy, electricity and
bandwidth)
* Equity Derivatives Panel w/discussion on accounting treatment and
U.S. commodity law changes
* Derivatives E-Trading and E-Business influence on derivatives
discussions

This year's AGM offers a variety of exciting social events. ISDA is inviting
key Members of Congress and regulatory staff to all of the following evening
events.

  Tuesday, April 3, 2001, from 7:30-10:30 p.m., Bank of
America, Goldman, Sachs & Co., J.P. Morgan, Merrill Lynch & Co., Inc., and
Morgan Stanley Dean Witter will host a welcoming reception at the Corcoran
Gallery of Art, 500 17th St., NW.  Noted jazz musician, Glen Pearson will
provide the evening's entertainment of jazz, blues and swing music.

  Wednesday, April 4, 2001 from 7:30-10:00 p.m., Bank of
America, Goldman, Sachs & Co., J.P. Morgan, Merrill Lynch & Co., Inc., and
Morgan Stanley Dean Witter will host a cocktail reception and buffet dinner
in the Great Hall at the Library of Congress, 10 1st St., SE.  The
"Strolling Strings" will provide an "around the world" music review.

  Thursday, April 5, 2001, from 7:00-10:30 p.m., Blackbird
will host a cocktail reception and buffet dinner at the Smithsonian National
Air and Space Museum, Independence Avenue at 6th St., SW.  The Midnight
Movers will provide an exciting concert of R&B, Soul and Motown music.

Hope you will be able to attend.  You can register online through the ISDA
website:  www.isda.org.  Thanks!

