Zooey note the below as you drive to Dallas on Friday.  Love, Dad. 


> Subject:	"OPERATION BLUE TALON 3:  CRASH CRACKDOWN"  LETTER FROM DOT,
> NATIONAL HIGHWAY TRAFFIC SAFETY ADMINISTRATION
> 
> 
> 
> The Environmental Health & Safety Department recently received the
> following letter from the Department of Transportation.  We hope each of
> you will take a minute to read it and help assist the DOT in their efforts
> over the holiday weekend.  Have a safe and happy holiday!
> 
> 
> "You can help prevent motor vehicle injuries and deaths by letting your
> employees, clients and vendors know about "Operation Blue TALON 3: Crash
> Crackdown," which will occur over the Labor Day weekend.
> 
> More than 74,000 law enforcement officers will join together to help
> prevent injury and death in motor vehicle crashes by enforcing traffic
> laws for occupant protection use, drinking and driving, aggressive
> driving, and exceeding speed limits.
> 
> Law enforcement officers will sweep Interstates 10, 30, 35, 40, and their
> feeder routes in the states of Texas, Arkansas, Louisiana, Oklahoma, New
> Mexico, and many of the Indian Nations.
> 
> This crash crackdown will begin at 6 p.m. Friday, August 31, and end at
> midnight Monday, September 3.  More than 1,600 municipal police, sheriffs,
> state police, and tribal law enforcement agencies will participate.
> 
> Highly publicized intensive enforcement periods such as these are
> effective ways to save lives by discouraging high-risk driving behaviors.
> Last year during "Operation Blue TALON 2: Crash Crackdown" in Region VI,
> Labor Day holiday fatalities decreased from 85 in 1999 to 55 in 2000, a 35
> percent reduction.  
> 
> Support for fair, effective enforcement of traffic safety laws is good for
> the community and good for business.  
> 
> We will appreciate your help.
> 
> Sincerely,
> 
> Georgia S. Chakiris
> Regional Administrator"
> 
> Bell Helicopter Textron Inc.
> Environmental, Health & Safety
> Ext. 12146

